## 4. Architecture

### 4.1 System topology

```
┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│  CONTROL LAYER                                                │
│  Stage 1: sclang (complete)                                   │
│  Stages 2+: Python process (mutation, bridge, MPE, UI)        │
│                                                               │
│  Responsibilities:                                            │
│  - FrequencySet state (list of ratios)                        │
│  - Mutation engine (Sethares roughness)                       │
│  - Anchor drone + two-group set arp (MIDI rig)                │
│  - MPE pitch-bend math (one channel per bus)                  │
│  - Loop transport / buffer management                         │
│  - UI / MIDI button handling                                  │
│  - Sends OSC to scsynth                                       │
│  - Sends MPE MIDI to IAC Bus 1/2 → Ableton                    │
└─────────────┬────────────────────────────┬────────────────────┘
              │ OSC                        │ MIDI (MPE via IAC)
┌─────────────▼────────────────┐  ┌────────▼─────────────────────┐
│  AUDIO SERVER (scsynth)       │  │  ABLETON LIVE                 │
│                               │  │                               │
│  In: MiniFuse 2 (2 ch)        │  │  - Audio input: BlackHole 16ch│
│  SoundIn(0,1) → Tartini →     │  │  - MPE synth tracks           │
│    AutotuneCh0/1              │  │  - VST/AU hosting             │
│  LoopBuf[N] → Tartini →       │  │  - Final mixing, monitoring   │
│    AutotuneLoop[N]            │  │  - Anchor drone + set arp     │
│  Granular FX bus              │  │                               │
│                               │  │  Output: MiniFuse 2/headphones│
│  Out: BlackHole 16ch (16 ch)  │  │                               │
└─────────────┬────────────────┘  └───────────────────────────────┘
              │ audio (ch 1–16)
┌─────────────▼─────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│  VIRTUAL ROUTING LAYER                                          │
│  BlackHole 16ch (audio) + IAC Driver (MIDI)                    │
│  No Aggregate Device: scsynth uses inDevice/outDevice directly │
└────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

### 4.2 Audio channel mapping (Stage 5, implemented)

SC output bus indices are 0-based; Ableton hardware input channels are 1-based.

| SC output bus | Ableton track | Ableton input ch | Content |
|---|---|---|---|
| 0–1 | 1 | 1/2 | Live autotuned stereo mix (Stage 4 current audio) |
| 2–3 | 2 | 3/4 | Loop 1 (reserved — Stage 8) |
| 4–5 | 3 | 5/6 | Loop 2 (reserved — Stage 8) |
| 6–7 | 4 | 7/8 | Loop 3 (reserved — Stage 8) |
| 8–9 | 5 | 9/10 | Loop 4 (reserved — Stage 8) |
| 10–11 | 6 | 11/12 | Granular FX (Stage 9, reserved) |
| 12–13 | 7 | 13/14 | Dry/diagnostic (reserved) |
| 14–15 | 8 | 15/16 | Reserved (future) |

The same map is machine-readable in `config/ableton_routing.json`. Stage 5
verifies the 16-channel infrastructure with test tones. Stage 4 live/loop audio
remains on pair 0/1 (Ableton track 1) for the first sound check. The loop and
granular pairs are reserved for later routing (Stage 8 for loop
transport/routing and Stage 9 for granular FX), not delivered as per-loop tracks in Stage 5.

### 4.2.1 Live-rig four-channel map (Stage 5.5, implemented)

`test_live_rig.scd` is the immediate product map: four **mono** outputs on the
first four BlackHole channels.

| SC output bus | Ableton track | Ableton input ch | Content |
|---|---|---|---|
| 0 | 1 | 1 | autotuned input 0 (mic) |
| 1 | 2 | 2 | autotuned input 1 (guitar) |
| 2 | 3 | 3 | loop 1 (autotuned playback) |
| 3 | 4 | 4 | loop 2 (autotuned playback) |

The map is machine-readable in `config/live_rig_routing.json`. It deliberately
differs from the Stage 5 8-pair infrastructure map above: here the two live
channels are separate mono signals, and the two loop voices have their own
channels. Loops 3/4 (optional Stage 4 extras) sum into SC 2/3. The Python
`/ji/freqset/update` receiver and lookup are unchanged.

